<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Did the Rockets Extend Jabari Smith Jr.?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Smith is paid <strong>$23.64m</strong> because he is a 6’11” forward who shoots from distance and defends, and Houston extended him before he could reach the market.</p>
<ul>
<li>A forward that size who can guard several positions and shoot threes is the most sought after shape in the modern game.</li>
<li>He went third in 2022, so his rookie contract alone paid <strong>$40.33m</strong> before this one started.</li>
<li>His scoring has stayed in the mid teens, which is why the figure stops short of a maximum.</li>
<li>He has missed stretches with a hand injury, and durability affects what a club will commit.</li>
<li>Nothing in the five years is optional, so Houston carries the whole commitment.</li>
</ul>
<p>He turned 23 in May, the youngest player on this roster earning more than <strong>$20m</strong>.</p>

