<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/jabari-smith-jr/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/jabari-smith-jr/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jabari Smith Jr.’s 2026-27 Salary?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Smith earns $23.64m in 2026-27, fourth on the Houston payroll and the first year of his extension. It is almost double the $12.35m he was paid last season. His career earnings come to $63.97m across five seasons, all at Houston. The salary is 11.80% of the club’s $200.41m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Jabari Smith Jr. Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Four seasons remain after this one, worth about $98.36m and all fully guaranteed. He reaches unrestricted free agency in the summer of 2031 at 28, which is the age at which a forward signs his largest contract."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Jabari Smith Jr. Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $23.64m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jabari Smith Jr.’s Contract With the Rockets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Smith signed a rookie extension on July 6, 2025, five years and $122m with every dollar guaranteed and no options at either end. It takes effect this season and runs to 2030-31, when he will be 27. Third overall in 2022 carries a large rookie contract on its own, and this deal is worth three times that again."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jabari Smith Jr.’s Net Worth in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Smith’s net worth is estimated at around $25.6m, derived from his $63.97m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. He played one season at Auburn and was 19 when Houston drafted him third in 2022. His father played four seasons in the league."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Did the Rockets Extend Jabari Smith Jr.?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Smith is paid $23.64m because he is a 6’11” forward who shoots from distance and defends, and Houston extended him before he could reach the market. He turned 23 in May, the youngest player on this roster earning more than $20m."}}]}</script>
